<p>Hi,</p>

<p>
  An Attend API token
  <% if @token_name.present? %>
    (<strong><%= @token_name %></strong>)
  <% end %>
  <% if @token_kind == "event" && @event_name.present? %>
    for the event <strong><%= @event_name %></strong>
  <% end %>
  <% if @token_kind == "series" && @series_name.present? %>
    for the <strong><%= @series_name %></strong> series
  <% end %>
  was just <strong>revoked</strong> using the token revocation endpoint.
</p>

<p>
  This happens when someone submits the token's secret value to
  <code>/api/v1/tokens/revoke</code> — typically because the token was leaked or
  exposed. The token no longer works, and any integration using it will stop
  functioning until you issue a replacement.
</p>

<p>
  <strong>If this was you,</strong> no further action is needed — you can create a
  new token from the event's Integrations page, the series' API Keys page, or the
  global API tokens page.
</p>

<p>
  <strong>If this was not you,</strong> your token secret may have been exposed.
  Revoking it was the right outcome, but you should review where the token was
  stored and rotate any related credentials.
</p>

<p>— Attend</p>
